  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist, and the rule is enabled and reporting status `ok`.\n\n**Data exploration**\n- The data view has request fields (`response`, `bytes`, `clientip`, `extension`, `url`, `geo.dest`) and a `timestamp` time field.\n- Responses are only `200` (12,832 requests), `404` (801), and `503` (441). The only 5xx code present is `503`.\n- Traffic comes mostly from CN (2,621), IN (2,323), and US (1,120).\n- The data spans 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03. Part of that range is after today (2026-10-12), so the dashboard uses an explicit range of 2026-10-01 to 2026-12-31 instead of the default last 7 days.\n\n**Dashboard: `EFF-0cd52b25 Web logs overview`**\n- Total requests (count metric)\n- Unique client IPs (unique count of `clientip`)\n- Requests over time (line, date histogram)\n- Responses by status code (bar, terms on `response.keyword`)\n- 5xx responses (ES|QL metric, `response.keyword LIKE \"5*\"`, currently 441)\n\n**Alert rule: `EFF-0cd52b25 5xx spike`**\n- Type `.es-query` on `kibana_sample_data_logs`, checked every 1 minute.\n- Counts documents where `response.keyword` matches `5*` over the last 5 minutes, and fires when the count is greater than 10.\n- Enabled, with no action connector attached, so it fires silently. Tell me if you want a connector such as Slack or email added.\n\nSome choices I made that you may want to change:\n- I used a wildcard query on `response.keyword` instead of the ES|QL rule type, since the ES|QL form isn't supported by this API path in my tools.\n- The 5xx count panel is an ES|QL panel rather than a field-based one, because the field-based panel filters only support exact-match values.",
